  // engine-quick-tier-6: tried forcing a0 to (pointer uint64) at op 65 (the
  // high 64 bits of a GIF tag this same block writes as two halves) to
  // resolve its own "Failed load" error; it cascaded into six new "Failed
  // store" errors on a3/a1/a0 elsewhere in the same function instead of
  // clearing cleanly (ops 13, 15, 24, 37, 51, 70), the same shape as an
  // unmasked cascade rather than a fix. Reverted; op 65's own error is held
