  // runtime's own &+ 16 precedent), masked to a byte for a bare "~x
  // VERTICES" hex dump. No field in adgif-shader's own table names this
  // offset with any confidence (28 bytes in lands mid gs-reg64, not a
  // documented boundary), so this casts the pointer to the raw word width
  // the load itself already uses rather than guessing a field name.
  // Once that clears, the same per-fragment loop increment as
  // debug-merc-highres-runtime above fails next: ops 255/256 advance s4
  // (merc-fragment) and s5 (merc-fragment-control) by their own asize-of
  // results, the identical "add failed" shape, same fix.
